        "original_id": "ec01f6ac-1ac9-5799-a5e9-9656b640c6f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Kluge, Sidney Salkow, Kay Harris, William Tracy, George Watts\n- Films: Yesterday Girl, Tillie the Toiler\n- Topics: New German Cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Salkow was born on June 16, 1911, and he became an American film director, screenwriter, and television director who worked on more than 50 motion pictures.\n- Alexander Kluge was born on February 14, 1932, and he is a German author, philosopher, academic, and film director.\n- Tillie the Toiler is a 1941 American comedy film directed by Sidney Salkow and starring Kay Harris, William Tracy, and George Watts.\n- Yesterday Girl, also titled Abschied von gestern and translated as \"Farewell to Yesterday,\" is a 1966 New German Cinema film directed and written by Alexander Kluge.\n- Sidney Salkow died on October 18, 2000.",
